# What kiosk's terminal types: the reference kiosk driven by the
# kiosk flow, by keyboard alone - the same keys as Showcase's host test of
# the kiosk (kiosk/showcase-kiosk-screens/tests/kiosk.rs,
# the_qemu_script_s_keys_on_the_host). Each `serial` step is one burst of
# keys written to the debug UART's receive side - by NoWayOS's
# tools/qemu-test into QEMU's serial port, by tools/pi-run through the
# Pi 5's Debug Probe - after the screen it waits for. Escapes: \r Enter,
# \t Tab, \e[B Down, \x20 Space. Each screen starts with focus on its first
# control, but the idle warning, on its second: Yes, I am here.

wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
# Start.
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
# A name and a reference, then Next. Every name typed starts zqvj, and the
# reference is 9081726354, both of which the expect files forbid.
serial zqvj\t9081726354\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-choice
# The first topic, then Next.
serial \e[B\t\t\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-checkbox
# The agreement, then Next.
serial \x20\t\t\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-notice
# Continue.
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing review
# Change: back to the step before, then Continue to the review again.
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-notice
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing review
# Send: the service stand-in leaves the first attempt unanswered, so it
# fails when the submission times out (2 s later in QEMU's test image, 5 s
# on the Pi).
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing failed
# Try again: accepted a second later.
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing submitted
# Done, once the confirmation has counted down a second and drawn the
# countdown alone - the same moment in QEMU's test image and on the
# Pi, whose confirmations last 4 s and 10 s.
wait SHOWCASE: ui: countdown drawn alone: 46x47 px of the 1920x1080 screen
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
# The next person starts, types a name and cancels (the reference, then
# Cancel).
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
serial zqvjb\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: app: session 2 ended: cancelled
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
# The next starts, types a name and walks away: the idle warning, then the
# privacy reset (5 s and 3 s later in QEMU's test image; 15 s and 15 s on
# the Pi, where make pi-show shows them).
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
serial zqvjc
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing idle-warning
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
